cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "RAC-HRP: Regime-Adaptive Clustering Hierarchical Risk Parity"
message: "If you use this software or its pre-registered protocol, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Patel
    given-names: Om
abstract: >-
  A pre-registered empirical study of whether absorption-ratio-triggered
  re-clustering improves hierarchical risk parity portfolios under changing
  equity correlation regimes. Includes point-in-time CRSP universe construction
  with survivorship-bias reconstruction gates and a two-tier synthetic null gate.
keywords:
  - hierarchical risk parity
  - portfolio optimization
  - regime detection
  - absorption ratio
  - pre-registration
license: MIT
